  "notes": "Vanilla Elemental at 60: Flame Shock kept ticking, Lightning Bolt spammed the rest of the time, Chain Lightning taking over on 2+ targets, with Searing Totem or Magma Totem dropped depending on target count -- matching the community guide's 'totems up, Flame Shock up, then Lightning Bolt' summary. The fork's elemental_shaman/apls/default.apl.json is the starting point but its final two lines are not adapted as-is: it casts Chain Lightning (10605) with no target-count condition ahead of Lightning Bolt in the priority list, which would fire Chain Lightning on every single-target cast too since it has no ability cooldown of its own -- gated it on numberTargets >= 2 here instead. It also filled its Lightning Bolt line with rank 4 (915) rather than the top rank; used rank 10 (15208), the highest this build's spellconst has, since nothing here calls for downranking. Left out the preset's mana-percent-gated Earth Shock filler: this build's spellconst gives Chain Lightning a 6 second category_cooldown_ms that Flame Shock and Earth Shock also carry, and it is not clear from spellconst alone whether that ties the three into one shared cooldown category in this fork -- a concern for the validation job, not something to guess at here.",
